WEBVTT

00:33.458 --> 00:35.041
[wind whooshing]

00:49.208 --> 00:50.375
[blowing]

00:52.500 --> 00:55.250
[alarm beeping, switches off]

00:56.583 --> 00:58.999
[tent flap unzips]

00:59.000 --> 01:00.249
[groans softly]

01:00.250 --> 01:02.250
[wind whistling]

01:13.791 --> 01:18.541
[dramatic music building]

01:25.625 --> 01:28.750
[woman] Come on, the sun is out.
It's perfect.

01:29.333 --> 01:30.540
Come on, let's go.

01:30.541 --> 01:34.124
- Can you get up, please, please, babe?
- [man] Mm, okay.

01:34.125 --> 01:36.708
[moaning] Oh, babe, your breath.

01:37.791 --> 01:38.957
You love it.

01:38.958 --> 01:40.582
[woman chuckles]

01:40.583 --> 01:42.332
- Wake up.
- Okay.

01:42.333 --> 01:43.249
- Yeah.
- Hm.

01:43.250 --> 01:45.040
- Go away.
- Let's go. Yeah.

01:45.041 --> 01:47.290
- Leave me alone.
- Let's get going, come on.

01:47.291 --> 01:50.250
- [dramatic music continues]
- [wind whistling]

02:02.958 --> 02:05.166
[groans happily]

02:05.916 --> 02:06.833
[laughs]

02:10.125 --> 02:12.583
- [grunts]
- Hey! Easy now.

02:21.583 --> 02:22.915
[wind whooshes]

02:22.916 --> 02:25.040
[woman] Come on, old man. You got this.

02:25.041 --> 02:26.250
[exhales heavily]

02:27.833 --> 02:29.416
[howls]

02:31.250 --> 02:34.457
[howls]

02:34.458 --> 02:36.250
[howl echoing]

02:38.083 --> 02:39.624
[man] Damn, it's getting cold.

02:39.625 --> 02:41.790
[woman] That's just your Aussie ass.

02:41.791 --> 02:42.916
[man laughs]

02:47.208 --> 02:50.665
- You ready to get to the top?
- Not yet, baby.

02:50.666 --> 02:52.083
Let's go. [blows softly]

02:54.333 --> 02:56.291
- [man] Yeah! You got it.
- [woman grunts]

02:59.458 --> 03:00.458
[grunts]

03:05.916 --> 03:07.250
[groans]

03:09.625 --> 03:10.875
[man] No rush.

03:12.583 --> 03:13.665
[groans]

03:13.666 --> 03:14.666
[yells]

03:15.791 --> 03:17.374
[tense music playing]

03:17.375 --> 03:18.457
You're all good.

03:18.458 --> 03:22.707
It's the same goddamn spot every time.
Gonna be here forever.

03:22.708 --> 03:24.374
How can I help you?

03:24.375 --> 03:26.457
[woman panting]

03:26.458 --> 03:27.666
I'm good.

03:28.625 --> 03:31.207
I got this. I can… [breathing heavily]

03:31.208 --> 03:32.500
I can do this.

03:33.208 --> 03:34.625
[man] Just take your time.

03:35.833 --> 03:36.833
[exhales sharply]

03:37.750 --> 03:39.000
[wind whistling]

03:47.916 --> 03:48.916
[grunts]

03:49.791 --> 03:51.208
[breathes deeply]

03:51.708 --> 03:53.208
- [man] Nice.
- [yells]

03:54.125 --> 03:55.291
[yells in frustration]

03:56.416 --> 03:58.500
[tense, percussive music playing]

04:01.416 --> 04:02.375
[sighs]

04:04.958 --> 04:05.958
What?

04:06.458 --> 04:08.124
I reckon we should call it a day.

04:08.125 --> 04:09.874
It's the final pitch, Tommy.

04:09.875 --> 04:11.666
[grunts]

04:13.791 --> 04:14.791
[yells]

04:16.458 --> 04:18.083
[music fades]

04:18.666 --> 04:20.582
It'll still be there
in the morning, I promise.

04:20.583 --> 04:21.957
[thunder rumbles]

04:21.958 --> 04:24.707
Plus, there's a bit of shit weather
coming in. Have a look.

04:24.708 --> 04:26.332
[woman] Just give me one more try.

04:26.333 --> 04:28.874
We can both hit the top
and make tent well within an hour.

04:28.875 --> 04:31.040
I know we can do that.
I want to summit today.

04:31.041 --> 04:33.582
- [Tommy] That is exactly why--
- No, I want to summit today.

04:33.583 --> 04:35.915
That's exactly why
you have a climbing partner,

04:35.916 --> 04:38.541
so that someone can make the call
when one of you loses the plot.

04:39.708 --> 04:43.249
- So I'm making a call. Okay?
- [sighs]

04:43.250 --> 04:45.249
Sash, it's all good.

04:45.250 --> 04:47.707
It was beautiful climbing,
up until where you… [chuckles]

04:47.708 --> 04:49.000
Right until when it wasn't.

04:52.583 --> 04:54.666
[wind whistling]

04:57.291 --> 05:00.332
Just wondering whether we should
take a rain check tomorrow, that's all.

05:00.333 --> 05:02.499
Are you kidding me?
It's just a little weather.

05:02.500 --> 05:04.500
What's… What's going on?

05:05.250 --> 05:06.500
[Tommy] No, just…

05:07.458 --> 05:11.208
I just feel like sometimes
you rush it a little bit, that's all.

05:15.125 --> 05:17.250
[tent flapping loudly]

05:21.833 --> 05:23.166
Anything else?

05:24.916 --> 05:29.249
[sighs] I don't know how many more
of these trips I've got left in me.

05:29.250 --> 05:34.707
Look, don't get me wrong.
I love this. I love us. I love you.

05:34.708 --> 05:36.499
Stop it. You do this every time.

05:36.500 --> 05:39.249
You know, the climb gets tough,
and then all of a sudden,

05:39.250 --> 05:40.624
you start talking like this.

05:40.625 --> 05:42.582
No, I'm just talking about
slowing it down a bit,

05:42.583 --> 05:45.040
not doing so many extreme things.

05:45.041 --> 05:46.666
[softly] Oh my God.

05:51.000 --> 05:52.374
[Tommy] There's an old saying.

05:52.375 --> 05:54.499
Luck is like anything else
you take up the mountain.

05:54.500 --> 05:56.249
Eventually, it's gonna run out.

05:56.250 --> 05:57.875
You serious?

05:59.291 --> 06:03.165
You're gonna tell me your luck
has run out halfway up a mountain?

06:03.166 --> 06:05.124
If my lucky compass is saying I should--

06:05.125 --> 06:07.916
[Sasha] Oh my God.
Just stop with that fucking compass.

06:12.916 --> 06:14.333
[Tommy] I'm sorry, Sash.

06:15.916 --> 06:17.791
I'm just being a bit of a sook.

06:19.333 --> 06:20.499
Come here.

06:20.500 --> 06:22.500
[Tommy groans]

06:24.541 --> 06:26.250
Where does it hurt?

06:27.291 --> 06:28.374
[Tommy] Yeah, right there.

06:28.375 --> 06:30.082
- Right here?
- [Tommy] Yeah.

06:30.083 --> 06:33.375
[Tommy groans] Jesus.

06:34.875 --> 06:37.582
[Sasha] Promise me we'll be back
after the storm's passed.

06:37.583 --> 06:40.875
We'll get going first thing, okay?
I promise not to sleep in.

06:42.250 --> 06:44.707
- Is that a date?
- [Tommy chuckles]

06:44.708 --> 06:46.708
[wind howling]

06:55.791 --> 06:57.375
[rumbling crash]

06:59.875 --> 07:01.165
[loud thudding]

07:01.166 --> 07:04.499
- [foreboding music playing]
- [rubble clattering]

07:04.500 --> 07:07.291
- [Tommy] Get into the wall!
- [Sasha] Okay, okay, okay.

07:08.041 --> 07:09.582
[Tommy] Keep your head down.

07:09.583 --> 07:11.541
[rubble skidding]

07:14.875 --> 07:17.957
Okay. I want us to go down a little bit.

07:17.958 --> 07:20.457
It's a bit safer there
at that ledge, okay?

07:20.458 --> 07:21.541
[Sasha] Okay.

07:25.083 --> 07:26.707
- [Tommy] You all right?
- [Sasha] Yeah.

07:26.708 --> 07:28.332
You can go faster if you want.

07:28.333 --> 07:29.415
- Oh yeah?
- [Tommy] Yeah.

07:29.416 --> 07:30.957
Now you want me to go faster?

07:30.958 --> 07:32.874
- Yeah.
- [Sasha] All right.

07:32.875 --> 07:34.916
[rope whirring]

07:40.833 --> 07:42.083
[Tommy] You safe?

07:44.750 --> 07:46.499
[both groan]

07:46.500 --> 07:47.707
God.

07:47.708 --> 07:49.708
[foreboding music intensifies]

07:53.958 --> 07:54.999
[Tommy] Are you okay?

07:55.000 --> 07:57.249
Tommy! Get down here!

07:57.250 --> 07:58.874
Did you tie a knot for this rap?

07:58.875 --> 08:00.083
Yeah!

08:03.416 --> 08:05.832
[Sasha] Oh shit! Tommy, wait!

08:05.833 --> 08:07.582
- Just give me a sec.
- [crash]

08:07.583 --> 08:10.875
- [Tommy groans, screams]
- [Sasha] Tommy!

08:12.666 --> 08:13.583
No!

08:14.208 --> 08:15.666
Shit. [breathing heavily]

08:18.500 --> 08:20.166
Tommy!

08:24.541 --> 08:26.415
[panting]

08:26.416 --> 08:30.290
- [metal scrapes]
- [Sasha exclaims] Tommy, wake up!

08:30.291 --> 08:33.040
You're dragging us off the mountain!

08:33.041 --> 08:35.166
[rope creaking]

08:37.458 --> 08:38.624
[groans]

08:38.625 --> 08:41.541
I can't hold it any longer!

08:46.083 --> 08:47.415
[whimpers]

08:47.416 --> 08:49.375
[ominous music pulsating]

08:53.041 --> 08:54.333
[Sasha screams]

08:55.875 --> 08:57.166
[body thuds]

08:58.750 --> 09:00.999
- [music fades]
- [breathing raggedly]

09:01.000 --> 09:02.875
- [metal skids]
- [Sasha screams]

09:04.541 --> 09:06.958
[exhales] Oh!

09:09.458 --> 09:12.666
[ethereal music playing]

09:14.125 --> 09:16.625
[groaning]

09:23.458 --> 09:24.791
[cries out]

09:26.416 --> 09:28.416
[panting]

09:52.000 --> 09:53.500
[music fades]

09:54.458 --> 09:57.166
["Boogie Street" by Leonard Cohen
playing on stereo]

10:08.125 --> 10:09.500
["Boogie Street" continues]

10:10.125 --> 10:15.875
<i>♪ And I'm back on Boogie Street ♪</i>

10:25.666 --> 10:27.666
[brakes squeak]

10:28.625 --> 10:30.666
<i>♪ A cigarette ♪</i>

10:32.833 --> 10:35.458
<i>♪ And then it's time to go ♪</i>

10:37.833 --> 10:41.791
<i>♪ I tidied up the kitchenette ♪</i>

10:43.458 --> 10:47.291
<i>♪ I tuned the old banjo ♪</i>

10:49.125 --> 10:54.790
<i>♪ I'm wanted at the traffic jam ♪</i>

10:54.791 --> 10:58.500
<i>♪ They're saving me a seat ♪</i>

11:00.458 --> 11:03.083
<i>♪ I'm what I am ♪</i>

11:04.000 --> 11:09.415
<i>♪ And what I am
Is back on Boogie Street ♪</i>

11:09.416 --> 11:11.749
- [song stops]
- [insects chirping]

11:11.750 --> 11:15.083
[creature calling in distance]

11:33.375 --> 11:35.666
[pensive music playing]

11:41.541 --> 11:44.875
[Tommy] <i>It's just these climbs, man,
the big tough ones. It's just…</i>

11:45.500 --> 11:46.957
Takes a lot of ego, you know?

11:46.958 --> 11:50.000
If you're nice,
I'll share some of my ego with you.

11:52.666 --> 11:53.958
[sighs]

11:58.083 --> 12:01.333
- [music fades]
- [TV playing indistinctly]

12:19.625 --> 12:20.708
[door closes]

12:21.625 --> 12:22.958
- Hey.
- G'day.

12:24.750 --> 12:26.125
You going out alone?

12:27.125 --> 12:28.666
I wouldn't recommend it.

12:30.375 --> 12:32.665
People get lost in these woods
all the time.

12:32.666 --> 12:34.625
And here, they stay lost.

12:35.291 --> 12:37.125
Can you sign in for us?

12:39.500 --> 12:41.332
Just so we know where you're going.

12:41.333 --> 12:43.333
[pen scratching]

12:46.333 --> 12:47.666
[dog barking]

12:51.125 --> 12:54.040
[man 1] Tough luck. Tough luck.
That's yours.

12:54.041 --> 12:55.750
[man 2] That's the good stuff.

12:56.458 --> 12:58.416
That's the good shit, there.

13:00.666 --> 13:03.665
- Is that packed on?
- For you, it's quite packed on.

13:03.666 --> 13:05.790
- Here you go.
- All right, thank you.

13:05.791 --> 13:06.875
Take it easy.

13:09.083 --> 13:09.916
Hello.

13:12.791 --> 13:13.791
Hey.

13:15.875 --> 13:16.916
[laughs softly]

13:23.291 --> 13:24.708
You got everything you need?

13:25.916 --> 13:28.624
- [man 3] Hey.
- [cashier] Look out. Here's trouble.

13:28.625 --> 13:30.749
How's it going, Mel? Ready for some more?

13:30.750 --> 13:33.250
Oh, yeah. It's selling like hotcakes.

13:33.750 --> 13:34.583
Oh.

13:36.041 --> 13:39.540
- Have you tried it?
- Get real. I wouldn't feed that to my dog.

13:39.541 --> 13:41.000
Well, I think your dog's missing out.

13:41.791 --> 13:42.958
[man 1] Excuse me.

13:43.708 --> 13:44.791
Thank you.

13:45.666 --> 13:47.625
Don't you say "excuse me"
where you come from?

13:49.875 --> 13:51.791
Did you not hear me? I said thank you.

13:57.250 --> 14:00.291
[man 2] Where are you heading?
We could be your guides.

14:00.875 --> 14:02.458
We know the place real well.

14:03.000 --> 14:05.749
- I'm okay.
- We're just trying to be nice.

14:05.750 --> 14:07.500
I think she's okay, fellas.

14:08.583 --> 14:10.666
Looks like she got everything she needs.

14:13.958 --> 14:15.958
[exhales loudly]

14:17.083 --> 14:19.166
- [door opening]
- [bell dinging]

14:19.750 --> 14:22.125
Full tank on six.

14:25.041 --> 14:26.500
I'm sorry about that.

14:27.416 --> 14:29.832
I just thought
I should probably have a bit of a word.

14:29.833 --> 14:32.624
Yeah, you didn't need to. It's okay.

14:32.625 --> 14:33.750
Oh, okay.

14:35.000 --> 14:36.041
No worries.

14:37.458 --> 14:40.582
Thanks, Mel. I'll be back in a tick.
I'm just gonna bring the car around.

14:40.583 --> 14:42.625
[Mel] Yeah. Sixty.

14:46.541 --> 14:47.541
Ta.

14:52.958 --> 14:54.750
Can you add this?

14:58.125 --> 15:00.875
[engine idling]

15:11.708 --> 15:13.290
[chatter on radio]

15:13.291 --> 15:14.832
Hi, hello?

15:14.833 --> 15:17.708
Hi. Um, can you…?

15:18.375 --> 15:19.749
- [switches radio off]
- Hey.

15:19.750 --> 15:21.957
I'm trying to get to Grand Isle Narrows.

15:21.958 --> 15:23.290
- Yeah?
- My GPS is out. Yeah.

15:23.291 --> 15:25.250
- You here for the canyon?
- [Sasha] Yeah.

15:26.375 --> 15:27.375
Yeah.

15:29.041 --> 15:31.082
You want the easy way or the hard way?

15:31.083 --> 15:33.375
Just… the best way.

15:33.958 --> 15:37.290
- Okay. So, this is us.
- [Sasha] Mm-hm.

15:37.291 --> 15:38.582
[man] You make this left,

15:38.583 --> 15:40.957
then it's a bit of a dog leg,
then a straight 50Ks.

15:40.958 --> 15:42.457
Okay, that's easy.

15:42.458 --> 15:45.999
[man] Sorry, can I give you my advice?
Completely different.

15:46.000 --> 15:47.707
[chuckles]

15:47.708 --> 15:49.291
Start at Blackstone Bay.

15:49.875 --> 15:50.875
Here.

15:51.375 --> 15:54.999
- You go about nine Ks.
- [Sasha] Mm-hm.

15:55.000 --> 15:59.124
Just before you get to the split break,
you'll find the most amazing camping area.

15:59.125 --> 16:00.040
[Sasha] Okay.

16:00.041 --> 16:02.624
It's a bit of a well-kept secret,
right by the shore.

16:02.625 --> 16:04.875
- Oh, thanks.
- [man] You think you can handle that?

16:06.416 --> 16:07.874
Yeah, I think I can handle it.

16:07.875 --> 16:08.790
- [man] Okay.
- Okay.

16:08.791 --> 16:10.874
You're gonna love it.
The water's unbelievable.

16:10.875 --> 16:13.082
- Okay, great. I really appreciate it.
- [engine starts]

16:13.083 --> 16:15.333
Okay. Just one more thing to think about.

16:16.083 --> 16:19.249
You know… I hope you know what
you're doing, 'cause it can get intense.

16:19.250 --> 16:21.415
- Intense, I know. It's okay.
- [man] Pretty gnarly.

16:21.416 --> 16:22.874
Most people do it in pairs.

16:22.875 --> 16:23.790
[raises window]

16:23.791 --> 16:25.082
- I'm gonna go.
- Oh, okay.

16:25.083 --> 16:27.125
I wasn't suggesting that you and I do--

16:30.166 --> 16:32.166
[slow, dramatic music plays]

16:48.791 --> 16:50.791
[night chirping]

17:08.666 --> 17:11.666
- [vehicle approaching]
- [music playing faintly on stereo]

17:19.041 --> 17:20.625
[dogs barking]

17:25.083 --> 17:27.958
[heavy metal music blaring]

17:29.000 --> 17:30.083
[quietly] Fuck.

17:31.083 --> 17:32.082
[music stops]

17:32.083 --> 17:33.458
[man 1] That's her again.

17:35.458 --> 17:36.916
Do you want a beer, love?

17:38.208 --> 17:39.625
[sinister music playing]

17:40.541 --> 17:42.541
[rifles cock and uncock]

17:44.541 --> 17:46.458
I think she wants to be alone.

17:47.625 --> 17:49.208
[man 2] You string up the little one.

17:51.291 --> 17:53.249
- [dog barks, growls loudly]
- [Sasha] Oh…

17:53.250 --> 17:54.874
[man 2 laughs]

17:54.875 --> 17:57.375
Oi! Hey, easy.

18:08.750 --> 18:13.000
- [man 1] She's trying to get out.
- [man 2] Sorry, no backing out now, love.

18:14.458 --> 18:15.750
I'm talking to you.

18:20.083 --> 18:22.250
[sinister music continues]

18:26.833 --> 18:28.166
[door locks]

18:38.625 --> 18:39.833
[knocking on window]

18:46.958 --> 18:48.958
We're just trying to be nice.

18:51.625 --> 18:52.833
[door handle rattles]

18:54.125 --> 18:55.125
Okay.

19:04.041 --> 19:07.291
[sinister music continues]

19:11.875 --> 19:14.374
- [men laughing]
- [man 1] You're missin' the best bits.

19:14.375 --> 19:16.749
That's what happens
if you stay in the car all day.

19:16.750 --> 19:19.124
- Look at this beautiful thing.
- [man 3] Right.

19:19.125 --> 19:22.041
[man 2] Okay, let's go.
Diesel, Ripper, get in the truck.

19:23.625 --> 19:24.833
[truck doors close]

19:25.708 --> 19:27.708
[trucks drive off]

19:34.416 --> 19:37.166
- [music fades]
- [birds chirping]

19:51.958 --> 19:56.750
[tranquil music playing]

20:06.666 --> 20:08.750
[music turns thrilling]

20:23.916 --> 20:24.750
[Sasha] Ooh!

20:38.541 --> 20:39.541
[grunts]

20:48.000 --> 20:49.125
[yelps]

21:08.166 --> 21:09.000
[grunts]

21:14.916 --> 21:16.416
[music slows]

21:58.916 --> 22:00.083
[grunts]

22:20.583 --> 22:21.875
[creaks softly]

22:27.958 --> 22:30.041
[somber music playing]

22:42.125 --> 22:44.541
[somber music intensifies]

23:10.166 --> 23:13.165
- [insects chirping]
- [creatures calling]

23:13.166 --> 23:14.250
[music fades]

23:58.625 --> 24:01.708
[pensive music playing]

24:14.000 --> 24:16.790
- [loud screech]
- [wings flapping]

24:16.791 --> 24:17.833
[twig snaps]

24:18.833 --> 24:20.833
[ominous music playing]

24:25.375 --> 24:26.708
[soft rustling]

24:54.375 --> 24:55.500
[softly] What?

25:00.125 --> 25:01.250
What the fuck?

25:04.333 --> 25:05.791
Where's my bag?

25:09.916 --> 25:10.916
Fuck.

25:17.416 --> 25:18.500
- [hisses]
- [Sasha gasps]

25:19.250 --> 25:20.541
Fuck! Fuck!

25:22.583 --> 25:23.416
[exhales]

25:24.458 --> 25:27.041
[breathing heavily]

25:28.500 --> 25:29.583
[hisses]

25:34.333 --> 25:37.166
[mysterious music playing]

26:27.083 --> 26:28.875
- [twig snaps]
- [wings flapping]

26:30.416 --> 26:33.125
[music darkens]

26:55.125 --> 26:56.166
Hello?

27:09.083 --> 27:10.500
[water splashes in distance]

27:14.666 --> 27:15.791
Hello?

27:18.708 --> 27:20.375
Ah! Hey!

27:21.000 --> 27:22.207
Hey.

27:22.208 --> 27:23.707
[man] You made it!

27:23.708 --> 27:25.624
It's me, from the gas station.

27:25.625 --> 27:27.665
[Sasha] Yeah, I remember.

27:27.666 --> 27:28.624
I'm Ben.

27:28.625 --> 27:30.374
Sasha, Ben. Nice to meet you.

27:30.375 --> 27:31.665
[Ben] Hi, Sasha.

27:31.666 --> 27:33.665
Hey, Blackstone Bay.

27:33.666 --> 27:36.249
What'd I tell you?
Dumps you right in the brown.

27:36.250 --> 27:38.625
- Mm-hm. Yeah.
- [Ben] You having fun?

27:39.291 --> 27:41.457
Yeah, the runs are great. I just, um…

27:41.458 --> 27:45.165
Something got into my gear last night
and took everything. My phone, my food.

27:45.166 --> 27:48.124
Oh, bloody hell. That's no good.

27:48.125 --> 27:50.291
Your mobile phone bill's
gonna be through the roof.

27:51.416 --> 27:53.957
Yeah, it's the wombats.
They're texting all the time.

27:53.958 --> 27:55.249
They text constantly.

27:55.250 --> 27:57.874
Yeah, that's a little wombat paw
working the key,

27:57.875 --> 27:59.207
in case you hadn't noticed.

27:59.208 --> 28:01.333
[both laughing]

28:02.041 --> 28:05.374
Seriously, though, I'm sorry.
It's a drastic bummer.

28:05.375 --> 28:08.540
I thought I hung it up high enough,
but guess not.

28:08.541 --> 28:10.540
No such thing out here, I'm sorry to say.

28:10.541 --> 28:13.583
Good news is I always pack
twice what I need.

28:14.291 --> 28:16.707
- I'm more than happy to suit you up.
- Really?

28:16.708 --> 28:17.790
Yeah, of course.

28:17.791 --> 28:19.915
That's what you gotta do out here.
You gotta share.

28:19.916 --> 28:22.124
No other way we all stay alive.

28:22.125 --> 28:24.416
Thanks, Ben. That's really great.

28:25.458 --> 28:26.541
You hungry?

28:27.541 --> 28:29.457
- Just kinda looking for that gear.
- Sit down.

28:29.458 --> 28:31.290
- Let me get you some fish.
- I would really--

28:31.291 --> 28:33.416
Please, I insist. Sit down.

28:33.958 --> 28:36.207
- Okay.
- Yeah, just there. Take a seat.

28:36.208 --> 28:38.583
Eat some food, get the gear, and then go.

28:44.166 --> 28:45.291
[grunts]

28:46.833 --> 28:48.625
[Ben] Yeah, here we go.

28:49.708 --> 28:51.582
So you make beef jerky?

28:51.583 --> 28:52.791
Uh, yeah.

28:53.666 --> 28:56.375
Yeah, I make that myself.

28:58.250 --> 28:59.125
Cut it.

28:59.833 --> 29:00.875
Dry it.

29:01.708 --> 29:04.707
Hang it away from the flies
for a few weeks.

29:04.708 --> 29:06.000
Good protein.

29:07.333 --> 29:11.082
It's not bad. I had some last night.
It's actually really good.

29:11.083 --> 29:12.708
- You tried Jenno's?
- Mm-hm.

29:13.541 --> 29:15.499
Why "Jenno's," by the way?

29:15.500 --> 29:17.125
It was my mum's name.

29:18.291 --> 29:19.624
Named it after her.

29:19.625 --> 29:21.582
You named beef jerky after your mom?

29:21.583 --> 29:22.999
Yeah.

29:23.000 --> 29:25.750
Well, she must be really flattered.
[laughing]

29:29.375 --> 29:31.166
Water. Want something to drink?

29:36.500 --> 29:40.375
Ever seen this before?
It's water siphoned from a tree.

29:43.833 --> 29:45.166
Pretty cool, huh?

29:53.791 --> 29:56.500
Don't worry,
I forgot to pack my roofies. [snickers]

29:58.250 --> 30:00.000
Come on, you gotta hydrate.

30:01.583 --> 30:03.625
Yeah, got to hydrate.

30:04.333 --> 30:05.665
Oh yeah.

30:05.666 --> 30:07.791
That usually impresses people.

30:08.791 --> 30:10.290
Yeah, it's impressive.

30:10.291 --> 30:11.291
Right?

30:12.333 --> 30:13.166
Yeah.

30:14.625 --> 30:15.625
Okay, so…

30:17.708 --> 30:19.332
Spend a lot of time out here?

30:19.333 --> 30:22.290
Oh yeah.
Yeah, I practically live out here.

30:22.291 --> 30:26.291
It's like I'm in pain if I don't get out
on the river once or twice a week.

30:27.083 --> 30:29.000
It's almost physical, you know?

30:30.166 --> 30:31.250
That need.

30:32.250 --> 30:33.999
Where in Australia are you from?

30:34.000 --> 30:36.749
Technically, not from Australia.

30:36.750 --> 30:39.083
No, I come from somewhere
far less appealing.

30:39.666 --> 30:42.332
My mum brought me out here
when I was a kid.

30:42.333 --> 30:44.291
Let me guess. Britain?

30:48.041 --> 30:51.541
- Fuck off. I guessed?
- Yeah, you guessed right.

30:52.500 --> 30:54.791
Uh, how long you been kayaking for?

30:55.333 --> 30:56.249
Mm?

30:56.250 --> 30:58.499
Oh, just a while.
I do a little bit of everything.

30:58.500 --> 30:59.415
Ah!

30:59.416 --> 31:01.250
But mostly mountains, right?

31:03.458 --> 31:05.333
So, I already know about you.

31:06.333 --> 31:08.874
Yeah, you know,
the danger makes you feel alive.

31:08.875 --> 31:12.124
Gotta be in the moment, or you may die.
Perfection's the only option.

31:12.125 --> 31:14.665
All that bullshit
they tell people like us.

31:14.666 --> 31:17.332
Personally, I think
your wiring's just messed up.

31:17.333 --> 31:19.666
You can fight your way
through a lot of shit,

31:20.791 --> 31:22.208
but you can't beat your wiring.

31:23.750 --> 31:26.083
Ain't no mountain high enough, right?

31:28.416 --> 31:29.416
Here you go.

31:30.333 --> 31:31.500
I'm done with mountains.

31:32.708 --> 31:34.250
[Ben] That's interesting.

31:35.208 --> 31:36.874
Let me guess.

31:36.875 --> 31:38.416
You broke up,

31:39.500 --> 31:43.624
and your boyfriend got the mountains,
and you got the rivers.

31:43.625 --> 31:45.125
Am I right?

31:49.208 --> 31:50.375
Oh shit.

31:51.250 --> 31:54.124
- I didn't mean to pry, Sasha. I'm so…
- No, it's fine.

31:54.125 --> 31:55.916
[Ben] I was just trying to be funny. I…

31:56.416 --> 31:58.999
That's the cost
of spending so much time alone.

31:59.000 --> 32:02.375
You completely lose the ability
to function in polite society.

32:03.583 --> 32:06.040
I know what that feels like.
That's why I'm out here.

32:06.041 --> 32:06.958
[Ben grunts]

32:07.708 --> 32:09.957
Don't have to playact like a human being.

32:09.958 --> 32:13.999
[laughs] Yeah. Yeah, there's enough noise
in the world, right?

32:14.000 --> 32:15.333
Speaking of noise,

32:15.833 --> 32:18.333
you know who showed up
at my campsite the other night?

32:19.208 --> 32:20.875
Those hunters from the gas station.

32:21.916 --> 32:23.708
They were definitely messing with me.

32:24.250 --> 32:26.125
Yeah, that's a little concerning.

32:26.708 --> 32:27.750
[Sasha] I know.

32:29.375 --> 32:30.750
[Ben] Assholes.

32:31.750 --> 32:32.791
It's fine.

32:33.416 --> 32:36.207
[Ben] You know,
most hunters aren't like that.

32:36.208 --> 32:41.249
The good ones respect the wilderness,
and we make use of what we kill.

32:41.250 --> 32:44.291
It's not about having an excuse
to drink with your buddies.

32:45.041 --> 32:46.790
It's more reverent than that.

32:46.791 --> 32:49.332
- [Sasha] Yeah, they weren't reverent.
- [Ben] No.

32:49.333 --> 32:50.874
They were trying to scare me.

32:50.875 --> 32:53.333
[Ben] Yeah, no, it sounds that way.

32:55.333 --> 32:57.250
You handled them perfectly, though.

32:59.625 --> 33:00.540
What?

33:00.541 --> 33:02.958
You had grit and poise.

33:03.708 --> 33:06.874
Amazing. You didn't give them an inch,

33:06.875 --> 33:09.457
but you didn't give them
an excuse to hurt you either.

33:09.458 --> 33:11.207
I'm… I'm sorry, what are you saying?

33:11.208 --> 33:12.625
[Ben] At the campsite.

33:13.250 --> 33:16.540
No, I was there.
I thought maybe you could use a hand.

33:16.541 --> 33:20.166
A woman alone and all.
Not the case, though, clearly.

33:20.750 --> 33:22.541
[laughing]

33:23.708 --> 33:25.875
Nah, you're special, Sasha.

33:26.500 --> 33:27.875
Just like my mum.

33:29.125 --> 33:31.250
I could sense it the moment we met.

33:31.791 --> 33:34.124
[sinister music playing]

33:34.125 --> 33:36.333
You're not gonna finish your brekkie?

33:36.958 --> 33:39.290
- Would you like me to wrap it up?
- [Sasha] That's okay.

33:39.291 --> 33:41.540
I'm just gonna get out of here.

33:41.541 --> 33:43.208
Hey, Sasha, what?

33:46.708 --> 33:47.958
Right.

33:49.166 --> 33:50.083
Yeah, this.

33:54.875 --> 33:56.707
I just fancied it.

33:56.708 --> 33:58.291
You want it back?

33:58.833 --> 34:01.333
No? Okay.

34:06.541 --> 34:09.000
I should go, Ben. It's time.

34:12.166 --> 34:13.458
[Ben] Don't forget your bag.

34:15.583 --> 34:17.625
[sinister music intensifies]

34:28.416 --> 34:29.332
[stereo beeps]

34:29.333 --> 34:32.583
["Go" by The Chemical Brothers
playing on speaker]

34:37.000 --> 34:40.458
So, I've restocked
your provisions and supplies.

34:41.125 --> 34:44.790
I've kept your phone, but I threw in
a few extras to level the playing field.

34:44.791 --> 34:46.208
You got the right shoes on?

34:48.041 --> 34:49.457
You'll be fine.

34:49.458 --> 34:50.832
So look, it's very simple.

34:50.833 --> 34:53.999
You've got until the very end of this song
to get as far away from me as you can.

34:54.000 --> 34:56.207
Okay?

34:56.208 --> 34:57.832
[Sasha breathing shakily]

34:57.833 --> 34:59.041
[Ben] What's the matter?

35:01.375 --> 35:02.916
I thought you liked danger.

35:03.416 --> 35:05.415
<i>♪ Everything gettin' harder to find ♪</i>

35:05.416 --> 35:07.415
<i>♪ Everybody jumpin' out of they mind ♪</i>

35:07.416 --> 35:08.957
<i>♪ Everybody goin' out of they skins ♪</i>

35:08.958 --> 35:10.040
<i>♪ See we get to the end ♪</i>

35:10.041 --> 35:11.666
<i>♪ But that's where we begin
You feel it … ♪</i>

35:12.291 --> 35:13.624
[screeches menacingly]

35:13.625 --> 35:15.332
<i>♪ Breakin' out and we breakin' the codes ♪</i>

35:15.333 --> 35:16.915
<i>♪ Similar to the Jacques Cousteau ♪</i>

35:16.916 --> 35:19.915
<i>♪ To the depths and you're wet
So your tank explodes, so get it out ♪</i>

35:19.916 --> 35:21.290
<i>♪ Send your body to flight ♪</i>

35:21.291 --> 35:22.999
<i>♪ Everybody got a target tonight… ♪</i>

35:23.000 --> 35:24.874
[song fades]

35:24.875 --> 35:27.249
<i>♪ All you studs and you duds
And you ladies, let's fly ♪</i>

35:27.250 --> 35:28.207
<i>♪ Grip the moment… ♪</i>

35:28.208 --> 35:30.374
[song continues in the distance]

35:30.375 --> 35:31.791
[Sasha panting]

35:34.750 --> 35:35.665
[grunts]

35:35.666 --> 35:36.875
[song continues loudly]

35:38.250 --> 35:40.250
<i>♪ No time to rest ♪</i>

35:40.833 --> 35:42.250
[song continues faintly]

35:46.250 --> 35:48.332
<i>♪ What you hear is not a test ♪</i>

35:48.333 --> 35:51.790
[softly] Yes! Yes! Yes! Yes!

35:51.791 --> 35:53.500
[song continues faintly]

35:55.375 --> 35:56.749
<i>♪ Go! ♪</i>

35:56.750 --> 35:58.750
[song ends]

36:00.833 --> 36:02.875
[ominous music builds]

36:04.000 --> 36:06.583
[intense music playing]

36:07.791 --> 36:09.458
[exclaims fearfully]

36:16.708 --> 36:18.166
[grunting]

36:47.541 --> 36:49.457
[Sasha exclaims, grunts]

36:49.458 --> 36:51.458
[muffled groaning]

36:58.666 --> 36:59.875
[gasps]

37:04.666 --> 37:05.833
[Sasha coughs]

37:20.500 --> 37:21.833
[coughs]

37:25.375 --> 37:27.375
[retches, coughs]

37:37.083 --> 37:38.624
[coughs]

37:38.625 --> 37:40.750
[insects chirping]

37:56.750 --> 37:59.166
[water splashes]

38:02.416 --> 38:04.416
[bleak music playing]

38:34.875 --> 38:36.499
[woman] <i>Yeah, I reckon it was.</i>

38:36.500 --> 38:37.957
[kid 1] <i>I mean, it could've been.</i>

38:37.958 --> 38:40.083
[man] <i>Let's stay focused on the job.</i>

38:46.041 --> 38:48.040
<i>Look at the birds, up there. Check it out.</i>

38:48.041 --> 38:48.957
[kids exclaim]

38:48.958 --> 38:49.999
Hello?

38:50.000 --> 38:53.624
[woman] <i>Hey, I actually reckon
you two are picking this up really well.</i>

38:53.625 --> 38:54.790
Hello?

38:54.791 --> 38:56.040
[kid 1] <i>Go by Dad's cookbook.</i>

38:56.041 --> 38:57.707
[man] <i>I'm gonna knock it out of the park.</i>

38:57.708 --> 38:59.874
- [woman] <i>Oh yeah?</i>
- [kid 2] <i>Yeah, with rancid fish?</i>

38:59.875 --> 39:02.749
[man] <i>You just wait.
I happen to be quite a bush craftsman.</i>

39:02.750 --> 39:04.624
<i>Are you going to catch a platypus?</i>

39:04.625 --> 39:06.790
- [woman] <i>Yeah.</i>
- [kid 2] <i>Yeah.</i>

39:06.791 --> 39:07.790
[man] <i>How cool is this?</i>

39:07.791 --> 39:10.499
[woman] <i>I know.
Look at those beautiful trees.</i>

39:10.500 --> 39:13.165
- [kid 1] <i>Trees, my eye.</i>
- [Ben on video] <i>Hey, Carters.</i>

39:13.166 --> 39:15.040
[Carters] <i>Hi, Ben!</i>

39:15.041 --> 39:16.791
<i>Hey!</i> [laughing]

39:17.958 --> 39:19.915
- [arrow whistles]
- [tree bark clattering]

39:19.916 --> 39:21.916
[Sasha panting]

39:23.166 --> 39:25.166
[foreboding music playing]

39:31.541 --> 39:33.458
[music intensifies]

39:52.583 --> 39:54.375
- [arrow whistles]
- [Sasha gasps]

40:01.208 --> 40:03.124
Fuck. Fuck.

40:03.125 --> 40:04.125
[screams]

40:07.166 --> 40:08.750
[trills, yips]

40:12.000 --> 40:14.000
[panting]

40:28.541 --> 40:29.875
- [arrow whistles]
- [Sasha yells]

40:35.416 --> 40:38.000
[Sasha screaming]

40:41.250 --> 40:43.000
[yells, grunts]

40:44.458 --> 40:47.000
[yelling, screams]

40:47.916 --> 40:50.916
[dark music playing]

40:54.541 --> 40:55.916
[gasping]

41:04.791 --> 41:06.000
[inhales sharply]

41:17.500 --> 41:19.083
[gasps, grunts]

41:43.291 --> 41:45.041
[music turns somber]

41:48.625 --> 41:52.125
- [birds chirping]
- [creatures calling]

41:59.583 --> 42:00.791
[exhales]

42:41.375 --> 42:43.416
[driving, percussive music plays]

42:52.125 --> 42:55.083
[music pulsates intensely]

43:00.750 --> 43:02.416
[Sasha panting]

43:14.666 --> 43:16.666
[music turns eerie]

43:47.583 --> 43:48.916
[grunts]

43:57.875 --> 43:58.875
[grunts]

44:14.333 --> 44:16.333
[somber music plays]

45:02.541 --> 45:03.625
[music fades]

45:06.875 --> 45:08.875
[panting softly]

45:15.541 --> 45:16.750
[exhales sharply]

45:18.208 --> 45:20.790
- [Ben screeches]
- [wings flapping]

45:20.791 --> 45:22.290
[birds calling urgently]

45:22.291 --> 45:24.375
[tense music plays]

45:31.125 --> 45:32.875
[tense, dramatic music plays]

45:56.250 --> 45:57.291
[exclaims]

45:58.458 --> 46:00.416
[low growling]

46:07.541 --> 46:09.208
[screeches like raptor]

46:11.416 --> 46:13.416
[tense, dramatic music continues]

46:28.416 --> 46:29.875
[Ben hoots]

46:37.458 --> 46:38.541
[faint rustle]

46:39.333 --> 46:41.333
[footsteps depart]

46:43.750 --> 46:44.958
[music fades]

46:45.708 --> 46:46.750
[grunts]

46:47.250 --> 46:48.291
[exhales]

47:04.666 --> 47:06.625
[panting]

47:20.458 --> 47:24.166
[breathing heavily]

47:28.833 --> 47:31.749
["Nasty Boy" by Trabant playing distantly]

47:31.750 --> 47:34.415
<i>♪ I'm a nasty little boy ♪</i>

47:34.416 --> 47:36.499
<i>♪ I'm a little useless ♪</i>

47:36.500 --> 47:39.332
<i>- ♪ I'm a useless little toy ♪</i>
- [Ben whoops]

47:39.333 --> 47:43.499
<i>♪ I'm a little useless
I'm a useless little toy ♪</i>

47:43.500 --> 47:44.666
<i>♪ Ow! ♪</i>

47:47.458 --> 47:49.458
[song grows louder]

47:50.708 --> 47:51.958
[Ben cackles]

47:53.958 --> 47:55.624
<i>♪ You're a little crazy ♪</i>

47:55.625 --> 47:57.750
<i>♪ You're a crazy little sexy girl ♪</i>

47:58.666 --> 48:00.624
<i>- ♪ You're a little crazy ♪</i>
- [Ben whoops]

48:00.625 --> 48:03.457
<i>♪ You're a crazy little sexy girl ♪</i>

48:03.458 --> 48:07.707
<i>♪ I can turn you on all night long ♪</i>

48:07.708 --> 48:10.457
<i>♪ I can turn you on
Wanna be your boy ♪</i>

48:10.458 --> 48:11.708
[music distorts]

48:17.583 --> 48:19.625
[music continues normally]

48:23.041 --> 48:24.957
<i>♪ I'm a little filthy ♪</i>

48:24.958 --> 48:27.041
<i>♪ I'm a filthy little dog ♪</i>

48:27.875 --> 48:29.624
<i>♪ I'm a little filthy ♪</i>

48:29.625 --> 48:32.707
<i>♪ I'm a filthy little horny dog ♪</i>

48:32.708 --> 48:36.790
<i>♪ I can turn you on all night long ♪</i>

48:36.791 --> 48:39.790
<i>♪ I can turn you on
Wanna be your boy… ♪</i>

48:39.791 --> 48:40.707
[Sasha groans]

48:40.708 --> 48:44.083
<i>♪ …your nasty, nasty, nasty little boy ♪</i>

48:46.333 --> 48:47.290
<i>♪ I'm your nasty… ♪</i>

48:47.291 --> 48:48.332
[wood cracks]

48:48.333 --> 48:49.624
[screams]

48:49.625 --> 48:50.957
[Sasha yells]

48:50.958 --> 48:53.540
<i>♪ N-n-n-nasty boy ♪</i>

48:53.541 --> 48:54.625
[song fades]

48:56.000 --> 48:57.250
[trap creaks]

48:58.000 --> 48:59.000
[groaning]

49:03.291 --> 49:05.125
[Ben yips, cackles]

49:11.166 --> 49:12.083
[Ben growls]

49:14.000 --> 49:15.541
[Sasha moaning]

49:17.375 --> 49:19.624
- [Ben yells]
- [bear spray spraying]

49:19.625 --> 49:21.083
[Ben shouting]

49:23.125 --> 49:24.750
[menacing music plays]

49:26.375 --> 49:27.875
- [Ben exclaims]
- [Sasha whimpers]

49:31.041 --> 49:32.708
[coughs]

49:37.791 --> 49:38.750
[Ben yells]

49:39.875 --> 49:41.416
[Ben laughs maniacally]

49:43.708 --> 49:45.540
[Ben grunts] Uh-uh-uh-uh!

49:45.541 --> 49:47.125
[Ben laughs]

49:48.083 --> 49:50.540
[Ben groaning]

49:50.541 --> 49:52.000
Oh, you got me.

49:52.666 --> 49:54.290
Toss the pepper spray.

49:54.291 --> 49:55.875
[menacing music continues]

49:57.083 --> 49:58.250
Okay.

49:59.166 --> 50:02.541
Okay, yeah. Okay, let's get this off you.

50:03.500 --> 50:04.957
On your tummy.

50:04.958 --> 50:07.665
It's okay. It's gonna be okay.

50:07.666 --> 50:09.791
Let's get this off you. Eyes forward.

50:12.291 --> 50:13.957
[Sasha groans]

50:13.958 --> 50:15.208
- [trap snaps shut]
- [Ben] Oh!

50:17.041 --> 50:18.083
Okay.

50:21.833 --> 50:22.916
Oh…

50:26.666 --> 50:27.750
Are you playing a game?

50:32.666 --> 50:35.749
Is that what you think we're doing?
You think we're playing a game, Ben?

50:35.750 --> 50:37.041
[Ben] It's not a game.

50:38.083 --> 50:39.665
It's a ritual.

50:39.666 --> 50:41.666
[foreboding music playing]

50:44.666 --> 50:48.875
- [rope creaking]
- [Sasha grunting]

50:52.250 --> 50:54.250
[music continues]

51:22.708 --> 51:24.541
[Ben] Hey! Hey, hey, don't.

51:47.666 --> 51:48.916
[music fades]

51:51.041 --> 51:52.375
You don't like being tied up?

51:54.041 --> 51:56.500
There's something
seriously wrong with you.

51:57.916 --> 51:59.125
[Sasha sighs]

52:05.500 --> 52:07.500
Now, come on, I gave you a choice.

52:08.833 --> 52:10.958
"You want the easy way or the hard way?"

52:12.708 --> 52:14.832
What did you choose? [ grunts]

52:14.833 --> 52:16.665
[Sasha groans softly] Mm.

52:16.666 --> 52:19.207
Let me know
when you reach your pain threshold.

52:19.208 --> 52:20.541
[Sasha groans]

52:21.291 --> 52:23.541
Don't disappoint me, Sasha.

52:25.833 --> 52:28.333
- [menacing music builds]
- [Sasha breathing deeply]

52:37.875 --> 52:39.875
[dark music playing]

52:51.958 --> 52:54.041
Rituals are very important.

52:55.041 --> 52:56.416
They ground us.

52:57.666 --> 52:59.750
They remind us of who we are.

53:03.916 --> 53:06.832
Did you know there are tribes
that file down their own teeth

53:06.833 --> 53:08.000
to sharp points?

53:10.291 --> 53:11.291
Hm?

53:12.875 --> 53:16.000
Enduring pain is a part
of growing up, Sasha.

53:17.291 --> 53:19.250
It's a rite of passage.

53:24.291 --> 53:26.291
[music intensifies]

53:42.666 --> 53:44.166
[music fades]

53:44.833 --> 53:46.250
Where are we going, Ben?

53:48.291 --> 53:49.625
I'll tell you later.

53:53.375 --> 53:56.375
You don't want to explain
the rules to me this time?

53:58.625 --> 54:02.208
I got your name from the ranger's register
and did a bit of a search.

54:05.416 --> 54:07.083
So the Troll Wall…

54:09.791 --> 54:11.958
I guess you don't wanna talk about that.

54:17.375 --> 54:19.625
It was just an unfortunate accident.

54:20.333 --> 54:23.375
Yeah, but I read online
that he was really experienced.

54:24.041 --> 54:27.958
He made some gnarly summits.
Doesn't really make sense.

54:28.625 --> 54:30.416
Things can always happen.

54:31.416 --> 54:34.083
[Ben] Yeah, I guess
nobody gets it right every time.

54:34.750 --> 54:37.625
I think it's the mental challenge
you gotta be ready for.

54:38.458 --> 54:40.500
You gotta be mentally prepared.

54:41.083 --> 54:43.207
That's it. I think you're right, Ben.

54:43.208 --> 54:46.166
- [Ben] Yeah.
- [Sasha] I absolutely agree with you.

54:47.083 --> 54:48.999
It's all in your mind, right?

54:49.000 --> 54:51.708
- Yeah, it's all in the mind, right?
- Yeah.

54:52.750 --> 54:54.791
What about the funeral.
Was it hot or cold?

54:58.583 --> 55:00.249
He was cremated.

55:00.250 --> 55:02.458
So did you come here to scatter his ashes?

55:03.041 --> 55:06.166
You're bringing the Aussie home.
He was from around here, right?

55:06.666 --> 55:09.125
[tense music plays]

55:15.166 --> 55:16.583
- [Sasha yells]
- [Ben laughs]

55:17.875 --> 55:20.291
Okay. [laughing]

55:23.291 --> 55:26.500
Uh-uh-uh! Stay there. Stay there.

55:27.208 --> 55:28.291
[gasps sharply]

55:31.958 --> 55:34.125
[grunts, whoops exuberantly]

55:34.750 --> 55:36.125
[Sasha gasps]

55:36.708 --> 55:38.333
[tense music continues]

55:46.583 --> 55:47.916
[inhales sharply]

55:54.958 --> 55:56.916
[music slows]

55:58.458 --> 56:01.041
[muffled groaning]

56:01.625 --> 56:03.291
[gasping]

56:07.916 --> 56:09.958
[panting]

56:22.500 --> 56:23.874
[music fades]

56:23.875 --> 56:26.416
[birdsong]

56:42.458 --> 56:43.500
Why?

56:45.250 --> 56:46.791
So you can get down there.

56:48.458 --> 56:50.000
[Ben taps harness] Put it on.

56:51.500 --> 56:53.458
[ominous music playing]

56:57.166 --> 57:00.208
- [water dripping]
- [harness creaking]

57:30.708 --> 57:35.416
[unsettling music playing]

57:39.958 --> 57:41.500
[Sasha gags, groans]

57:52.208 --> 57:54.416
[ominous sting]

58:01.208 --> 58:02.125
[Sasha gasps]

58:02.958 --> 58:05.957
There are native tribes that say

58:05.958 --> 58:09.916
to capture the spirit of your prey,
you have to consume its liver.

58:10.541 --> 58:13.708
The trick is finding a spirit
worth capturing, I suppose.

58:16.333 --> 58:18.750
You remember the Carters from the video?

58:20.041 --> 58:22.208
They didn't put up much of a fight.

58:23.291 --> 58:24.916
Not like you.

58:26.083 --> 58:29.541
I try to take as much care
and attention as possible.

58:32.541 --> 58:34.708
At the end of the day,
they're all human beings.

58:35.291 --> 58:37.916
And it's important
to make use of the kill.

58:39.166 --> 58:40.916
Every part of it.

58:41.500 --> 58:42.833
Nothing goes to waste.

58:44.708 --> 58:46.250
[Sasha breathing sharply]

58:47.875 --> 58:49.625
[Ben] It's more reverent that way.

58:50.375 --> 58:51.416
Am I right?

58:52.000 --> 58:53.790
Oh my! [groans]

58:53.791 --> 58:58.165
- Oh my God. No!
- You must be exhausted from the journey.

58:58.166 --> 59:00.874
- No, no, no! [whimpering]
- [Ben] Why don't you take a rest?

59:00.875 --> 59:03.040
Come on, yeah, it's okay.

59:03.041 --> 59:05.375
- [Sasha] No!
- Come on, come to my bedroom.

59:06.458 --> 59:07.458
Yeah.

59:08.666 --> 59:09.999
Yeah.

59:10.000 --> 59:11.124
[Sasha groans]

59:11.125 --> 59:13.041
[Ben, sighing] Oh!

59:13.625 --> 59:17.000
[Sasha exclaims, breathing heavily]

59:20.375 --> 59:22.083
Hey, can I ask you something?

59:25.333 --> 59:27.708
[softly] You really think
I've got a problem?

59:29.791 --> 59:31.791
[unsettling music playing]

59:38.000 --> 59:39.000
I think…

59:41.375 --> 59:43.500
I think people hurt you.

59:45.708 --> 59:47.791
And they did bad things to you.

59:49.458 --> 59:50.458
Uh…

59:52.791 --> 59:56.124
And I'm so sorry
those things happened to you, Ben.

59:56.125 --> 59:57.750
- I can't imagine what…
- [Ben sighs]

01:00:06.750 --> 01:00:07.875
[Ben groans]

01:00:16.666 --> 01:00:18.416
[breath trembles]

01:00:30.250 --> 01:00:32.375
[chain rattles]

01:00:45.041 --> 01:00:46.208
[Sasha] Please, stop.

01:00:50.750 --> 01:00:51.833
[tense sting plays]

01:00:55.791 --> 01:00:57.791
[breathing shakily]

01:01:10.083 --> 01:01:11.083
Ben?

01:01:15.666 --> 01:01:16.666
Ben?

01:01:20.541 --> 01:01:21.624
[Ben screeches]

01:01:21.625 --> 01:01:23.582
- [ominous music playing]
- Oh, no!

01:01:23.583 --> 01:01:25.333
- No! No!
- [Ben snarling]

01:01:26.958 --> 01:01:28.916
[both grunting]

01:01:56.625 --> 01:01:58.291
Do you know what this is?

01:01:59.541 --> 01:02:00.375
Hm?

01:02:01.208 --> 01:02:04.124
This is my homemade salt brine.

01:02:04.125 --> 01:02:05.749
[liquid sloshes]

01:02:05.750 --> 01:02:08.291
It's a perfect tenderizer.

01:02:08.958 --> 01:02:11.583
It's a very important part of the process.

01:02:18.333 --> 01:02:20.375
The photo next to your bed?

01:02:23.500 --> 01:02:25.041
Is that your mom?

01:02:26.583 --> 01:02:28.750
She looks just like you.

01:02:33.708 --> 01:02:34.833
Yeah.

01:02:46.375 --> 01:02:49.582
[Sasha breathing heavily]

01:02:49.583 --> 01:02:52.000
[softly] Do you know
what she used to say to me?

01:02:56.416 --> 01:02:59.291
"Jenno loves Benno."

01:03:01.750 --> 01:03:04.165
"And Benno loves Jenno."

01:03:04.166 --> 01:03:06.000
- [Sasha laughs awkwardly]
- Yeah.

01:03:10.750 --> 01:03:12.333
She was special.

01:03:14.041 --> 01:03:16.500
She was the first one.

01:03:25.458 --> 01:03:26.916
Do you understand?

01:03:30.041 --> 01:03:32.250
Now she's always with me.

01:03:36.333 --> 01:03:38.291
I'm gonna keep you with me too.

01:03:43.541 --> 01:03:45.165
[Sasha] You're a sick fuck.

01:03:45.166 --> 01:03:46.791
[Ben screams]

01:03:54.833 --> 01:03:56.333
- [Ben grunts]
- [Sasha screams]

01:03:57.375 --> 01:03:59.958
- [fabric rips]
- [Ben grunting]

01:04:01.000 --> 01:04:02.000
[Sasha grunts]

01:04:04.791 --> 01:04:06.083
[Ben] Sasha!

01:04:08.125 --> 01:04:09.750
[Sasha yells]

01:04:12.250 --> 01:04:13.541
[frenetic music playing]

01:04:24.583 --> 01:04:25.625
[Sasha screams]

01:04:26.708 --> 01:04:29.832
[gasping desperately]

01:04:29.833 --> 01:04:31.000
[yells]

01:04:31.791 --> 01:04:33.125
[Ben yells]

01:04:37.250 --> 01:04:41.291
[terrifying music playing]

01:04:45.125 --> 01:04:46.458
[Ben] Sasha!

01:04:47.791 --> 01:04:48.874
Sasha!

01:04:48.875 --> 01:04:50.208
[gasps]

01:04:57.833 --> 01:04:59.250
[Sasha screams]

01:05:07.083 --> 01:05:08.125
[cable creaks]

01:05:24.375 --> 01:05:25.583
[muffled groan]

01:05:32.750 --> 01:05:33.833
[muffled groaning]

01:05:38.625 --> 01:05:40.000
[muffled screams]

01:05:54.625 --> 01:05:57.333
[gasps, panting heavily]

01:06:03.041 --> 01:06:05.125
[tense music playing]

01:06:16.250 --> 01:06:17.416
[Sasha grunts]

01:06:32.291 --> 01:06:33.458
[groans softly]

01:06:35.958 --> 01:06:37.041
[strained grunt]

01:06:40.875 --> 01:06:42.415
[Sasha screams]

01:06:42.416 --> 01:06:43.749
[gasps]

01:06:43.750 --> 01:06:44.749
Fuck.

01:06:44.750 --> 01:06:45.583
[coughs]

01:06:47.125 --> 01:06:49.125
[Sasha yelling]

01:06:52.750 --> 01:06:53.708
[Sasha yells]

01:06:57.458 --> 01:06:59.666
[tense music continues]

01:07:01.791 --> 01:07:03.249
[both grunting desperately]

01:07:03.250 --> 01:07:04.375
[Sasha yells]

01:07:06.458 --> 01:07:07.625
[grunts]

01:07:18.166 --> 01:07:21.416
[both grunting]

01:07:30.875 --> 01:07:32.541
[grunting animalistically]

01:07:41.833 --> 01:07:42.666
[low growling]

01:07:43.416 --> 01:07:44.958
[breathing deeply]

01:07:46.833 --> 01:07:48.333
[gasps]

01:07:49.083 --> 01:07:50.291
[coughs]

01:07:51.833 --> 01:07:52.666
It's okay.

01:07:54.250 --> 01:07:55.083
[Ben groans]

01:07:58.583 --> 01:07:59.790
- [Sasha grunts]
- [Ben screams]

01:07:59.791 --> 01:08:00.790
[bone cracks]

01:08:00.791 --> 01:08:01.707
[Sasha screams]

01:08:01.708 --> 01:08:03.791
[Ben screams]

01:08:08.583 --> 01:08:09.625
[whimpers]

01:08:13.791 --> 01:08:16.040
[Ben groans loudly]

01:08:16.041 --> 01:08:18.915
- [Ben whimpering]
- [uneasy music playing]

01:08:18.916 --> 01:08:21.250
[pained grunting]

01:08:28.708 --> 01:08:32.208
[screams] You've broken my leg!

01:08:33.875 --> 01:08:36.500
[sobbing]

01:08:38.916 --> 01:08:40.166
[Ben screams]

01:08:41.708 --> 01:08:44.040
[Ben continues sobbing]

01:08:44.041 --> 01:08:46.416
[Sasha grunts, exhales]

01:08:47.083 --> 01:08:49.208
[Ben sobbing]

01:08:50.625 --> 01:08:54.458
- [eerie music playing]
- [Ben wailing]

01:09:26.583 --> 01:09:28.540
[mosquito buzzing]

01:09:28.541 --> 01:09:30.541
[Sasha laughs dryly]

01:09:32.833 --> 01:09:35.291
People come here on vacation.

01:09:36.541 --> 01:09:37.458
[laughs]

01:09:41.208 --> 01:09:43.625
You must have one hell of a dentist.

01:09:47.625 --> 01:09:49.458
Or did you eat him too?

01:09:52.541 --> 01:09:53.500
[buzzing stops]

01:09:57.625 --> 01:09:59.166
[thunder rumbles]

01:10:01.291 --> 01:10:03.583
You ever get depressed in the dark?

01:10:10.750 --> 01:10:13.291
Feel like you misjudged things?

01:10:17.833 --> 01:10:19.166
Feel guilty?

01:10:25.666 --> 01:10:27.000
When he fell…

01:10:29.541 --> 01:10:32.333
he was dragging
both of us off the mountain.

01:10:34.541 --> 01:10:36.541
[solemn music plays]

01:10:40.083 --> 01:10:41.625
[softly] I had to let him go.

01:10:49.291 --> 01:10:52.250
I'll never know if he was still alive.

01:10:55.625 --> 01:10:58.583
I was only there because he was there.

01:11:00.375 --> 01:11:02.833
And he didn't want to be there anymore.

01:11:03.708 --> 01:11:04.791
[laughs dryly]

01:11:07.000 --> 01:11:08.750
I didn't listen.

01:11:14.125 --> 01:11:15.875
I just kept pushing.

01:11:23.416 --> 01:11:25.458
[solemn music continues]

01:11:40.875 --> 01:11:42.875
[flies buzzing]

01:11:52.708 --> 01:11:54.291
What's back there, Ben?

01:11:55.625 --> 01:11:57.874
[Ben] About 12 days of walking.

01:11:57.875 --> 01:11:59.541
[Sasha] You'll never survive it.

01:12:00.041 --> 01:12:02.000
Yeah, and whose fault is that?

01:12:03.541 --> 01:12:05.916
I have to get
to the top of that wall today.

01:12:08.500 --> 01:12:10.708
We either get up there today…

01:12:13.291 --> 01:12:15.250
or I wait for you to die.

01:12:16.875 --> 01:12:20.208
And you will. From an infection.

01:12:20.791 --> 01:12:22.500
You can't climb it without me.

01:12:28.208 --> 01:12:29.208
Maybe.

01:12:31.333 --> 01:12:35.040
Maybe you're right. It is a tandem climb.

01:12:35.041 --> 01:12:36.500
Let's do it.

01:12:37.000 --> 01:12:38.625
Come on. Okay?

01:12:40.125 --> 01:12:41.625
Let's do it together.

01:12:45.583 --> 01:12:46.625
It's okay.

01:12:51.958 --> 01:12:54.749
I'm gonna tell you how to tie a knot

01:12:54.750 --> 01:12:57.458
with some of that rope
to make a booster for your good leg.

01:12:58.083 --> 01:13:00.083
And we'll build you a harness.

01:13:00.583 --> 01:13:03.457
A diaper harness.
It's the only way to get you up there.

01:13:03.458 --> 01:13:04.832
I've already got a harness.

01:13:04.833 --> 01:13:08.958
If I'm gonna lead this climb,
I can only do it with that harness.

01:13:13.875 --> 01:13:15.791
You can't do it, Ben.

01:13:17.250 --> 01:13:18.291
[sighs in distress]

01:13:22.125 --> 01:13:24.541
Take these off so I can help you.

01:13:28.958 --> 01:13:31.000
Do it over by the wall, okay?

01:13:35.958 --> 01:13:36.875
[Ben groans]

01:13:37.666 --> 01:13:38.666
Fuck.

01:13:46.041 --> 01:13:47.500
It needs to be tight.

01:13:49.166 --> 01:13:50.166
Tighter.

01:13:53.791 --> 01:13:54.916
Come here.

01:14:01.541 --> 01:14:03.207
Just so you know,

01:14:03.208 --> 01:14:06.499
when you get us to the top,
I'll set you free.

01:14:06.500 --> 01:14:10.541
But if you try to drop me,
then I will rip you off that wall.

01:14:11.583 --> 01:14:13.791
[tense music playing]

01:14:23.083 --> 01:14:25.125
Don't you dare touch this harness.

01:14:34.875 --> 01:14:37.290
[tense music continues]

01:14:37.291 --> 01:14:39.291
[birds cawing]

01:14:45.375 --> 01:14:46.250
[grunts]

01:14:52.416 --> 01:14:54.125
[screams]

01:15:17.666 --> 01:15:19.125
[groans]

01:15:32.916 --> 01:15:34.375
[groans]

01:15:41.541 --> 01:15:42.833
[exhales]

01:15:53.666 --> 01:15:55.083
[grunts]

01:16:20.000 --> 01:16:22.291
- [Ben] Hey!
- [Sasha screams]

01:16:23.708 --> 01:16:26.624
- Fucking idiot!
- I told you not to touch the harness!

01:16:26.625 --> 01:16:28.207
[Ben yells in pain]

01:16:28.208 --> 01:16:31.333
- I was just resetting it.
- Not the fucking leg!

01:16:32.041 --> 01:16:33.916
[Sasha grunts]

01:16:36.375 --> 01:16:38.416
[tense music continues]

01:17:08.250 --> 01:17:09.791
Hey, can I ask you something?

01:17:11.750 --> 01:17:13.082
When Tommy fell,

01:17:13.083 --> 01:17:15.291
did it look like he was flying?

01:17:34.250 --> 01:17:35.333
[groans]

01:17:36.291 --> 01:17:38.916
Yeah! Come on!

01:17:39.958 --> 01:17:42.375
[Sasha grunting, panting]

01:17:48.625 --> 01:17:50.083
Nice. Nice work.

01:17:52.958 --> 01:17:54.625
[whoops]

01:17:55.416 --> 01:17:56.541
Yeah!

01:17:58.750 --> 01:18:00.375
We make a good team, don't we, eh?

01:18:02.041 --> 01:18:03.250
You know what I mean?

01:18:04.958 --> 01:18:06.583
[bird screeches]

01:18:08.166 --> 01:18:10.250
[tense music continues]

01:18:16.000 --> 01:18:17.250
Hey, Sasha?

01:18:18.916 --> 01:18:20.416
[Sasha] All right. You're good.

01:18:23.666 --> 01:18:25.500
[creaks]

01:18:32.458 --> 01:18:33.875
[groans]

01:18:35.375 --> 01:18:36.416
Hey, what've you done?

01:18:37.458 --> 01:18:39.041
- Sasha!
- Ow!

01:18:40.541 --> 01:18:43.040
You promised me we'd do it together!

01:18:43.041 --> 01:18:44.624
[yells furiously]

01:18:44.625 --> 01:18:45.707
No!

01:18:45.708 --> 01:18:47.375
[both yelling]

01:18:48.666 --> 01:18:49.749
[Ben] Don't do it!

01:18:49.750 --> 01:18:51.082
[Sasha whimpering]

01:18:51.083 --> 01:18:53.708
- [Ben roars]
- [Sasha crying out]

01:18:57.333 --> 01:18:59.666
Sasha! [roars]

01:19:04.666 --> 01:19:06.666
[panting]

01:19:17.166 --> 01:19:18.416
[screams]

01:19:22.541 --> 01:19:23.625
[gasps]

01:19:25.916 --> 01:19:26.958
[exhales]

01:19:34.208 --> 01:19:36.833
- [solemn music plays]
- [birds cawing]

01:19:54.375 --> 01:19:56.375
[heartbeat thumping]

01:20:10.375 --> 01:20:11.999
[heartbeat fades]

01:20:12.000 --> 01:20:13.916
[wind whistling]

01:20:17.833 --> 01:20:20.791
[Sasha breathing heavily]

01:20:23.750 --> 01:20:25.833
[somber music plays]

01:20:49.541 --> 01:20:50.375
[softly] Okay.

01:20:53.458 --> 01:20:54.416
[groans]

01:20:56.291 --> 01:20:58.916
[groans, blows air]

01:21:08.083 --> 01:21:09.458
[exhales deeply]

01:21:12.666 --> 01:21:14.666
[music intensifies]

01:21:28.458 --> 01:21:31.166
[groaning softly]

01:21:34.208 --> 01:21:36.124
[screams]

01:21:36.125 --> 01:21:38.707
[yelling]

01:21:38.708 --> 01:21:40.791
[suspenseful music playing]

01:21:48.708 --> 01:21:49.583
[yells]

01:21:56.416 --> 01:21:59.125
[groans] Fuck!

01:22:01.208 --> 01:22:02.958
[panting]

01:22:05.500 --> 01:22:06.500
Okay.

01:22:14.208 --> 01:22:16.208
[dramatic music plays]

01:22:21.041 --> 01:22:22.333
[sighs]

01:22:23.750 --> 01:22:24.916
[groans]

01:22:29.208 --> 01:22:31.333
[breathes deeply]

01:22:41.125 --> 01:22:42.291
[grunts forcefully]

01:22:56.625 --> 01:22:59.375
Okay. [groans]

01:23:10.166 --> 01:23:11.375
[grunts]

01:23:19.500 --> 01:23:21.500
[panting]

01:23:31.416 --> 01:23:33.416
[breathing heavily]

01:23:41.333 --> 01:23:42.500
[moans]

01:23:46.166 --> 01:23:48.125
[panting]

01:23:54.750 --> 01:23:56.833
[laughs]

01:24:09.000 --> 01:24:11.000
[birds chirping]

01:24:14.291 --> 01:24:16.291
[grunts, exhales]

01:24:29.125 --> 01:24:31.250
[sobs softly]

01:24:52.750 --> 01:24:54.791
[water splashing]

01:25:08.708 --> 01:25:10.750
